# Cline Rules - Momentum Energy Dashboard

Project: Momentum Energy Dashboard, a Flutter app that visualises a customer''s
Momentum Energy (Australia) electricity usage from a downloaded CSV export.

## Commands
- `flutter pub get` - install/refresh dependencies.
- `flutter test` - run the test suite (aggregation logic + widget test).
- `flutter analyze` - static analysis. Pre-existing SDK deprecation/info
  warnings are expected; treat any NEW error as a regression.

## Data source
- Unlike the Amber app, this one does NOT call an API. The user downloads a
  usage CSV from the Momentum Energy MyAccount Portal and uploads it in the
  app. The CSV is parsed and aggregated LOCALLY (in-browser / on-device); the
  file is never uploaded.
- Parsing uses the `csv` package (`CsvToListConverter`). The test fixture is
  `assets/Your_Usage_List_Sample.csv`.
- Source rows are 5-minute intervals (`METER_INTERVAL = 5`).

## Tests
- `test/bar_chart_test.dart` - `DataAggregator` aggregation tests. The ''1 Day''
  test asserts 48 half-hour bars and that each bar sums 6 x 5-minute values
  (e.g. 0.018 + 0.015 + ... + 0.019).
- `test/widget_test.dart` - basic widget smoke test.

## Chart aggregation model (IMPORTANT)
- Graph bars are FIXED **half-hour buckets**: 2 bars/hour = 48 bars/day. This
  is intentional and must NOT be changed to one-bar-per-interval.
- 5-minute data: **6 five-minute intervals are summed into each half-hour
  bar** (value = sum of 6 x 5-min kWh or cost).
- In `lib/bar_chart.dart`, `graphPos` uses
  `date.hour * 2 + date.minute ~/ 30` (half-hour width). This is correct; do
  NOT "fix" it to a per-interval formula (that would create 288 bars and
  produce wrong time ranges and values).
- The daily supply charge is split per interval
  (`DAILY / 24 / (60 / METER_INTERVAL)`) and summed back to a half-hour amount
  across the 6 intervals in a bar.

## Key constants (lib/bar_chart.dart)
- `METER_INTERVAL` = 5 (the 5-minute source interval).
- `DAILY` = daily supply charge; `CONTROLLED`, `OFFPEAK`, `SHOULDER`, `PEAK` =
  tiered rates used by `_getCost`; `colors` = bar segment colours.
- Tariff/time-of-use bands in `_getCost`/`_getCostColor` are keyed on `graphPos`
  in half-hour units (e.g. `graphPos < 7 * 2` = before 07:00).

## Versioning
- `pubspec.yaml`: `version: x.y.z+build` (e.g. `1.3.1+18`).

## Deployment
- No local deploy script. CI is Codemagic. **Push to `origin/master`** to
  trigger the build/deploy (web, Android, iOS). Configured via the Codemagic
  dashboard (no `codemagic.yaml` in the repo).

## Gotchas
- Test runs can fail with a locked build dir (`build\unit_test_assets`). Fix
  by deleting the build folder (`Remove-Item -Recurse -Force build`) and
  re-running `flutter test`.
- Repo files are **CRLF**. Multi-line edits via the editor tool using `\n`
  fail to match; prefer single-line edits or include `\r\n`.
- A plain `git push origin master` can falsely print "Everything up-to-date"
  even when the commit is still local. Use `git push origin master --verbose`
  to force a real push, then confirm with `git log origin/master`.
- `lib/utils.dart` `darken`/`lighten` may still use the deprecated
  `Color.red/green/blue/alpha` getters (SDK deprecation, not a logic bug).
